            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Persian for a rumour, then the Persian for to deny."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: قضاوت کردن",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "قضاوت کردن (qezâvat kardan) — \"to judge\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "او زود درباره دیگران قضاوت میکند. u zud darbâre-ye digarân qezâvat mikonad. She is quick to judge other people."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Qezâvat \"judgement\" + kardan (stem kon-). Darbâre-ye kasi qezâvat kardan — to judge someone. It also means to referee a match."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "قضاوت was borrowed from Arabic qaḍāwa \"judging\" (EtymDB), from the same Arabic family as qāḍī \"a judge\"; kardan \"to do\" is inherited Persian."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
            }
